# Citation metadata for MOVE OpenLab (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# Verified from the repository (2026-11-16): the author (pyproject.toml and every commit of the history), the
# affiliation (README › Maintainer), the version (src/move_openlab/__init__.py), the repository address, and the
# licence of the public framework (LICENSE, Apache-2.0); date-released is the date of the 0.3.1 release.
#
# Deliberately absent until they exist (never invent them):
#   - doi / identifiers: add them when a DOI is registered (for example by archiving a release);
#   - orcid of the author: add it once verified;
#   - preferred-citation: the platform paper, to add ONLY after its acceptance. Template (uncomment and complete):
#       preferred-citation:
#         type: article            # or conference-paper
#         title: "<title as published>"
#         authors:
#           - family-names: "BEN ATIA"
#             given-names: "Okba"
#         collection-title: "<proceedings or journal>"
#         year: <year>
#         doi: "<doi of the paper>"
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "MOVE OpenLab"
abstract: >-
  MOVE OpenLab: a reproducible experimentation framework for sustainable mobility optimization, conceived, designed,
  developed and implemented by Dr. Okba BEN ATIA. Problems, methods, metrics and datasets plug in through adapters;
  every solution is checked by an independent validator; experiments are frozen, exported as verified bundles,
  re-executed and compared claim by claim.
authors:
  - family-names: "BEN ATIA"
    given-names: "Okba"
    affiliation: "Université Marie et Louis Pasteur, FEMTO-ST Institute, DISC Department, OMNI team"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OkbaBenatia/move-openlab-framework"
keywords:
  - optimization
  - reproducibility
  - experimentation framework
  - benchmarking
  - independent validation
  - ride matching
  - sustainable mobility
